-- lmf.PTNOTE
COMMENT ON TABLE "lmf"."PTNOTE" IS 'This table provides information about the plot and any special considerations taken when collecting data.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."SURVEY" IS 'This field indicates the year of survey design; data collection may or may not have happened that year.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."STATE" IS 'Federal Information Processing Standard or Series (FIPS) code for the state; see STATENM table to look up FIPS codes for various states.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."COUNTY" IS 'Federal Information Processing Standard or Series (FIPS); see COUNTYNM table to look up FIPS codes for various counties.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."PSU" IS 'ID number for the rectangular area that is the first stage of the two-stage sample design. Each rectangle has three possible points in it, of which the field crews attempt to sample two.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."POINT" IS 'The number of the point within the rectangular PSU. The points are the second stage of the two-stage sample design. Field crews go to 1 first, then 2, and then 3 if one of the others failed.';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."PTSECTION" IS 'The "section" that the note corresponds to (e.g., soils, line point intercept). "noteBiomass": refers to the POINT table biomass collection (i.e. Standing Biomass protocol). "noteConcerns" refers to the CONCERN table. "noteDist" refers to the DISTURBANCE table. "noteEco" refers to the ESFSG table. "noteFieldPosition" refers to the POINTCOORDINATES table. "noteFieldVisit" refers to the POINT table and docuemnts site visit specific notes (e.g. access issues). "noteLanduseSource" refers to the LANDUSE field in the POINT table. "noteLnIntr" refers to the GINTERCEPT table (i.e. notes about the Gap Intercept protocol). "noteLoc" refers to the POINT table, documenting something specific about the location. "notePlantCensus" refers to the PLANTCENSUS table. "notePlantHeight" refers to PASTUREHEIGHTS table. "notePract" refers to the PRACTICE table. "noteProdPlots" refers to the POINT table TOT_ANN_PROD column and the Production method generally. "notePtIntercept" refers to the PINTERCEPT table. "noteRngHlth" refers to the RANGEHEALTH and RHSUMMARY tables (i.e. Rangeland Health protocol). "noteSagebrushShape" refers to the PINTERCEPT table SAGEBRUSH_SHAPE field. "noteSoils" refers to the SOILHORIZON table (i.e Landscape and Soils protocol). "noteStability" refers to the SOILDISAG tables (i.e. Soil Stability Test protocol). "unknownPlant[USDA PLANT CODE]" refers to the PLANTCENSUS table, and documents notes about a particular unknown plant, where USDA PLANT CODE is replaced by the plant code in question (e.g. unknownPlant2GP1, unknownPlant2FA1).';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."PTNOTE"."PTNOTE" IS 'Notes about a particular plot or method within the plot.';

-- lmf.RANGEHEALTH
COMMENT ON TABLE "lmf"."RANGEHEALTH" IS 'This table provides information about rating the 17 indicators of the Interpreting Indicators of Rangeland Health method';
COMMENT ON COLUMN "lmf"."RANGEHEALTH"."SURVEY" IS 'This field indicates the year of survey design; data collection may or may not have happened that year.';
